<%# English translation of privacy-content.ejs. Keep it in sync with the Greek original (same variables and conditions). %>
  <p class="alert alert-info small translation-note">This is a translation provided for convenience. In case of any discrepancy, the Greek version prevails. <a href="<%= locals.siteUrl || '' %>/privacy" hreflang="el">Read the Greek version</a>.</p>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p><%= company.legalName %><% if (company.vat) { %>, VAT No. <%= company.vat %><% } %><% if (company.gemi) { %>, GEMI No. <%= company.gemi %><% } %><% if (company.seat) { %>, <%= company.seat %><% } %>.
    For personal data matters: <% if (company.privacyEmail) { %><a href="mailto:<%= company.privacyEmail %>"><%= company.privacyEmail %></a><% } else { %>via our <a href="<%= u('/contact') %>">contact form</a><% } %>.</p>

  <h2>2. What data we process, why and for how long</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="table">
    <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th><th>Retention period</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Booking and performance of the rental contract</td><td>Full name, email, telephone, date of birth, driving licence details, flight, notes, child’s details for a child seat</td><td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td><td>Driving licence details, date of birth, telephone, flight, notes: <%= config.retention.operationalMonths %> months after the return, unless a damage claim or a traffic penalty notice is pending</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tax documents (myDATA) and accounting records</td><td>Full name/company name, VAT No. (for an invoice), amounts, dates</td><td>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c))</td><td>For as long as tax legislation requires</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Identifying the driver to the authorities for traffic offences committed during the rental</td><td>Driver and booking details</td><td>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c))</td><td>Until the offence has been dealt with</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Security deposit, damage, fraud prevention, evidence in payment disputes</td><td>Card type and last 4 digits, authorisation code, vehicle condition reports and photographs of the car, correspondence</td><td>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)): protecting our fleet and defending legal claims</td><td>Until the security deposit is settled and the related claims become time-barred</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Customer account</td><td>Email, password (encrypted), name, telephone</td><td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td><td>Until the account is deleted</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Replying to messages and complaints</td><td>Name, email, telephone, message</td><td>Legitimate interest / pre-contractual measures</td><td><%= config.retention.messagesMonths %> months</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p>Providing the booking details is necessary for concluding the contract; without them we cannot complete the booking. The checks on the driver’s age and years of holding a driving licence are carried out automatically on the basis of the published rules; you can contact us to have the decision reviewed by a person. We do not send marketing messages without your consent.</p>

  <h2>3. Card details</h2>
  <p>Card payments are made on the secure page of the payment provider (Stripe or Revolut) or on our bank’s POS terminal. <strong>We do not see or store the full number or the CVV of your card.</strong> For the security deposit we store only the card type (e.g. Visa credit), the last 4 digits and the authorisation code.</p>

  <h2>4. Recipients</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Payment providers: Stripe Payments Europe Ltd. and/or Revolut, and the bank that operates our POS terminal. The payment providers also act as independent controllers for their own obligations (e.g. fraud prevention).</li>
    <li>Website hosting and email delivery providers (processors, under a contract pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR).</li>
    <li>Our accountant and e-invoicing provider, and the Independent Authority for Public Revenue (AADE) (myDATA).</li>
    <li>The insurance company (in the event of damage or an accident), and the authorities (Traffic Police, municipalities) where required by law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Transfers outside the EEA</h2>
  <p>Some providers (e.g. the Stripe group) may process data in the United States. Such transfers take place on the basis of the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework or the European Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right of access to, rectification, erasure, restriction and portability of your data. You can download your data or delete your account from the ‘Account’ page, or write to us; we reply within one month. On deletion, we keep only what tax legislation requires or what relates to a pending claim.</p>
  <p><strong>Right to object (Article 21 GDPR):</strong> you may object at any time, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to processing based on our legitimate interest.</p>
  <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Hellenic Data Protection Authority (www.dpa.gr).</p>
  <p>Additional drivers are informed about the processing of their data by means of a printed notice at pick-up.</p>

  <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use <strong>only one strictly necessary cookie</strong>, <code>sid</code>, for signing in to your account, keeping forms secure and completing your booking. It lasts until you close your browser (or 30 days, if you select ‘Remember me’ when logging in). We do not use advertising or analytics cookies, so no consent is required.</p>
